insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b2-d344278f1953', 'en', 'B2', 'The Unexpected Journey: A Story of Second Chances', 'When Marta looked back on her life, she realized that the most significant changes often happened when she least expected them. Having grown up in a small town in Brazil, she had always dreamed of exploring the world. However, it wasn''t until she turned thirty that she finally gathered the courage to move to London. By that time, she had already finished her degree in business administration and had worked for seven years in a bank. Yet, she felt that something was missing.

Her first few months in London were challenging. She had studied English in Brazil, but she quickly discovered that understanding real conversations was much harder than reading textbooks. Every day, she would come home feeling exhausted and discouraged. But she persisted, attending language classes and practicing with her new friends. After six months, she had noticed a significant improvement in her fluency.

One rainy Tuesday, while waiting for the bus, she met an elderly Englishman named Mr. Thompson. They started talking, and he told her about his own adventures as a young man. He had traveled to India, Australia, and even Brazil in the 1960s. Marta was fascinated. Before she knew it, she had missed her bus, but she didn''t mind. By the time they said goodbye, she had exchanged contact information with him and had promised to visit him for tea the following week.

That visit was the beginning of a beautiful friendship. Mr. Thompson, who had never had children, treated Marta like a granddaughter. He shared his stories, his wisdom, and his love for literature. In return, Marta helped him with his computer and introduced him to Brazilian music. Through him, she met other elderly people in the neighborhood and started volunteering at a local community center. Life had taken an unexpected turn, and Marta felt happier than ever.

However, the pandemic hit in 2020, and everything changed. The community center closed, and Mr. Thompson, who was eighty-five, had to stay indoors. Marta, now a nurse, worked long hours at a hospital. By the time the lockdowns eased, Mr. Thompson had passed away. Marta was devastated. She had not been able to say goodbye, but she had cherished every moment they had spent together. She realized that those moments had taught her more about life than any textbook ever could.

Years later, Marta found herself back in Brazil, visiting her family. She had achieved many things since then, but she hadn''t forgotten Mr. Thompson. One day, she discovered an old letter in her drawer that he had written to her before he died. In it, he had written, ''Dear Marta, your arrival in my life was a blessing. Remember that every ending is a new beginning.''

Marta wiped a tear from her eye and smiled. She had never known about the letter, but now, reading his words, she felt a sense of peace. She realized that her journey had been full of twists and turns, but each step had brought her to where she was meant to be. She decided to honor his memory by writing a book about their friendship, hoping to inspire others to open their hearts to unexpected connections. She also began to reflect on how her initial struggles with the English language had transformed into a deep appreciation for the nuances of communication. In her free time, she started teaching English to recent immigrants in her community, using the same techniques that had helped her. By sharing her own story, she found that she could motivate others to embrace their own challenges. The memory of Mr. Thompson''s kindness and wisdom continued to guide her actions, and she often recounted his words to her students: ''Patience and persistence are the keys to unlocking any door.'' With every new person she helped, she felt that she was paying forward the generosity she had received. The manuscript she prepared was not just a tribute to Mr. Thompson, but also a testament to the power of human connection across cultures and generations.', '[{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz que ela tinha terminado sua graduação em administração e trabalhado em um banco por sete anos antes de se mudar.","options":["She had finished her degree and worked in a bank.","She had started a nursing course.","She had traveled around the world.","She had written a book."],"prompt":"What had Marta done before she moved to London?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Marta conheceu Mr. Thompson enquanto esperava o ônibus em uma terça-feira chuvosa.","options":["At the hospital where she worked.","At a community center.","While waiting for a bus.","At a language class."],"prompt":"How did Marta meet Mr. Thompson?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto menciona que ele compartilhou suas histórias, sabedoria e amor pela literatura.","options":["His knowledge of computers.","His stories, wisdom, and love for literature.","Brazilian music.","His experiences as a nurse."],"prompt":"What did Mr. Thompson share with Marta?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto afirma que Mr. Thompson faleceu depois que as restrições da pandemia começaram a diminuir.","options":["He moved to India.","He passed away.","He opened a community center.","He moved to Brazil."],"prompt":"What happened to Mr. Thompson during the pandemic?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Marta encontrou uma carta antiga que Mr. Thompson havia escrito para ela antes de morrer.","options":["A photo of Mr. Thompson.","A letter from Mr. Thompson.","A diary she had written.","A book she had started."],"prompt":"What did Marta find in her drawer years later?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Na carta, ele escreveu: ''Lembre-se de que todo fim é um novo começo.''","options":["He apologized for not saying goodbye.","He asked Marta to visit his grave.","He said every ending is a new beginning.","He asked Marta to come back to Brazil."],"prompt":"What did Mr. Thompson write in the letter?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Ela decidiu escrever um livro para honrar a memória de Mr. Thompson e inspirar outros a se abrirem para conexões inesperadas.","options":["To make money.","To honor Mr. Thompson''s memory.","To teach English.","To share her nursing experience."],"prompt":"Why did Marta decide to write a book?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A história destaca como a amizade inesperada com Mr. Thompson transformou a vida de Marta.","options":["The importance of technology.","The value of unexpected friendships.","The difficulties of learning a language.","The impact of the pandemic on elderly people."],"prompt":"What is the main theme of this story?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
