insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b2-4d74ae86ba31', 'en', 'B2', 'The Passive Voice in News: How Events Are Reported', 'When reading the news in English, you will often notice that the focus is on the event itself rather than on who performed the action. This is achieved through the passive voice, a grammatical structure that allows writers to emphasize the action or its receiver. For example, a headline might read "Relief Efforts Continue" without specifying who is continuing them. This is not a mistake; it is a deliberate choice to keep the report neutral or to highlight the consequence rather than the agent.

Consider the case of a recent educational policy in California. A judge delayed a decision on whether to stop the state from requiring high school students to pass an exit exam to graduate. The lawsuit was filed on behalf of students who argued that the test was unfair to those who had not received equal education. The passive voice is used here: "The lawsuit was filed" instead of "A law firm filed the lawsuit." This shifts the focus to the legal action itself and away from the lawyers who initiated it.

In another example, from Utah, a law was signed that legalized homebrewing of beer and wine. The passive construction "was signed" directs our attention to the law and the signing event, not to the governor who performed the action. Similarly, "the law was introduced by a representative" highlights the law''s introduction in the legislature rather than the representative''s personal involvement.

Passive voice is also common in reporting research findings. For instance, in a study about ambidextrous children, it was reported that these children are more likely to have problems at school. The passive construction "was reported" is used to attribute the information to an unnamed source, which is typical in academic and news writing. The children were studied over several years, and their language skills were assessed. The passive voice here emphasizes the children as the receivers of the assessment, not the researchers who conducted it.

Moreover, the passive voice is particularly useful when the agent is unknown or irrelevant. In news about disasters, we often read "Over 116,000 people were reported dead" without specifying who reported this. This is because the focus is on the tragic statistic, not on the source of the information. Similarly, "aid is being delivered" is a passive construction that focuses on the action of delivering aid, not on the organizations doing it.

In everyday communication, using the passive voice can sound more formal or impersonal. For example, saying "The decision was delayed" is more neutral than "The judge delayed the decision." However, overusing the passive voice can make your writing seem evasive, as it allows you to omit responsibility. It is important to know when to use it and when to prefer the active voice. For instance, in a news report about a political scandal, a journalist might write "Mistakes were made" to avoid blaming specific individuals, but if the goal is to hold someone accountable, the active voice is more direct: "The mayor made mistakes." Understanding this nuance is key to both interpreting and producing English in a professional setting.

To form the passive voice, you combine the verb ''to be'' with the past participle of the main verb. The tense of ''to be'' changes to indicate when the action happened. For example, in the present simple, we say "The exam is required"; in the past simple, "The decision was delayed." The agent can be introduced with ''by'', as in "The law was signed by the governor," but often it is omitted. Additionally, the passive voice can be used in different tenses, such as the present continuous "aid is being delivered" or the present perfect "the report has been published." Being able to recognize and use these forms will help you describe events with the appropriate level of detail and focus.

Mastery of the passive voice will greatly enhance your ability to understand and produce English at a B2 level. It will allow you to interpret news articles more accurately and to express yourself in a more nuanced and professional way. For example, when writing an email to a colleague about a missed deadline, you might say "The report was not submitted on time" to avoid sounding accusatory, whereas in a direct conversation you might say "You did not submit the report on time." Choosing the right voice is a skill that will serve you well in both formal and informal contexts.', '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A voz passiva é usada para enfatizar a ação ou o receptor da ação, em vez de quem a pratica. No jornalismo, isso ajuda a manter a neutralidade ou destacar o evento.","options":["To make the sentence longer","To focus on the action rather than the doer","To hide the identity of the writer","To confuse the reader"],"prompt":"What is the primary function of the passive voice in news reporting?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Na frase passiva, o agente (quem pratica a ação) é frequentemente omitido. Aqui, o agente é a firma de advogados, mas não é mencionado porque o foco está na ação de entrar com o processo.","options":["The students","The judge","The law firm","The state"],"prompt":"In the sentence ''The lawsuit was filed on behalf of students'', what is the agent (the doer) of the action?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A estrutura passiva usa o verbo ''to be'' + particípio passado. ''The law was signed'' é passiva, enquanto as outras opções estão na voz ativa.","options":["The governor signed the law.","The law was signed by the governor.","The governor is signing the law.","The governor has signed the law."],"prompt":"Which of the following sentences is in the passive voice?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A voz passiva é útil quando o agente é desconhecido ou irrelevante. Em desastres, o foco está nos danos, não em quem os causou.","options":["To make the victims seem responsible","To avoid mentioning the source of the damage","To make the sentence more active","To praise the rescue workers"],"prompt":"Why might a journalist choose the passive voice when reporting damage from a disaster?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"No passado simples, a passiva é formada com ''were'' + particípio passado. ''The children were studied'' está correta.","options":["The children were studied by the researchers.","The children are studied by the researchers.","The children had been studied by the researchers.","The children were being studied by the researchers."],"prompt":"What is the correct passive form of the sentence ''The researchers studied the children'' in the past simple?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"''is being'' indica presente contínuo na voz passiva. A ação está em andamento.","options":["Present simple","Present continuous","Past simple","Past continuous"],"prompt":"In the phrase ''aid is being delivered'', what is the tense of the passive voice?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto afirma que a voz passiva é particularmente útil quando o agente é desconhecido ou irrelevante, como em notícias sobre desastres.","options":["When the agent is unknown or irrelevant","When the agent is the main focus","When the sentence is too short","When the action is unimportant"],"prompt":"According to the text, when might a journalist choose to omit the agent in a passive sentence?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto menciona que usar a voz passiva pode soar mais formal ou impessoal, o que é uma vantagem em contextos formais.","options":["It makes the writing more lively.","It makes the writing sound more formal or impersonal.","It makes the writing less clear.","It always shortens the sentence."],"prompt":"What is one advantage of using the passive voice in formal writing?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, body=excluded.body, questions=excluded.questions, is_published=excluded.is_published, updated_at=now();

insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b2-1f8b86069add', 'en', 'B2', 'A Judge''s Delay: The Story Behind the Headlines', 'In the spring of 2006, a legal battle in California captured the attention of educators, students, and parents across the state. At the heart of the controversy was the California High School Exit Examination, a test that students had to pass in order to graduate. The case reached a critical point when a judge announced that he would delay his decision until Friday, leaving thousands of students in limbo.

The lawsuit had been filed on behalf of Liliana Valenzuela, a senior at Richmond High School, and others who argued that the test was unfair. They claimed that it violated the principle of equal protection, because students from poor backgrounds and those learning English did not have the same educational opportunities as their more privileged peers. The law firm Morrison & Foerster represented the students, contending that the exam perpetuated inequality.

On Monday, Judge Robert B. Freedman of the Alameda County Superior Court said he would issue an injunction against the test unless the state''s attorneys presented a convincing argument by 2 p.m. that day. The injunction would have stopped the state from requiring the test for graduation. However, instead of making an immediate decision, Freedman said he would wait until Friday to issue his ruling. This delay meant that thousands of seniors who had not yet passed the exam would have to keep waiting to find out their fate.

The number of affected students was significant. State Superintendent Jack O''Connell reported that about 47,000 seniors across California still needed to pass the test. Without a passing score, they would face the grim prospect of completing four years of high school without receiving a diploma. In the meantime, many students, including 32 from James Logan High School, were scheduled to take the second part of the exam on Wednesday.

The judge''s decision had far-reaching implications. Supporters of the exam argued that it ensured high standards and accountability. Critics, however, saw it as a barrier that punished students for circumstances beyond their control. The case highlighted a deep divide in educational policy, as well as the complex role of the courts in shaping school requirements.

As the community awaited the Friday ruling, students and educators alike reflected on the broader meaning of the test. Was it a fair measure of achievement, or an unfair hurdle? The judge''s delay only added to the tension and uncertainty. The final decision, whenever it came, would not only determine the immediate futures of thousands of seniors but also set a precedent for how standardized tests could be used in public education. Moreover, the debate extended beyond California, sparking conversations in other states about the efficacy and fairness of high-stakes testing. Educators nationwide watched closely, knowing that the outcome could influence their own policies. For many, the case became a symbol of the struggle between upholding rigorous standards and ensuring that no student is left behind due to circumstances beyond their control.

The story of the California exit exam is a reminder of how a single legal decision can have a profound impact on people''s lives. It also illustrates the delicate balance between maintaining educational standards and ensuring equity for all students. For those involved, the days of waiting were filled with anxiety and hope, as they waited to see what the judge would say. Students like Liliana Valenzuela, who had worked hard throughout high school, found themselves in a position where their entire future hinged on a legal ruling. Teachers and administrators were equally anxious, as their students'' achievements and their own professional judgments were called into question. The emotional toll was evident in the hallways of schools across the state, where conversations often turned to the test and its consequences.

In the end, the judge''s delay was more than just a postponement; it was a moment for the state to reconsider its position and for the public to engage in a vital conversation about fairness in education. The outcome would shape the experiences of countless students, and the debates it sparked would continue long after the decision was handed down. The case also prompted a reevaluation of how standardized tests are used, not only in California but across the nation, as educators and policymakers sought to find a balance between accountability and opportunity.', '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O processo alegava que o teste violava o princípio de proteção igual, pois estudantes pobres e aprendizes de inglês não tinham acesso igual à educação.","options":["The test was too difficult for most students.","The test was unfair to students from poor backgrounds and English learners.","The test was not required by the state law.","The test was administered without proper supervision."],"prompt":"What was the main reason the lawsuit was filed against the California High School Exit Examination?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto menciona que o escritório de advocacia Morrison & Foerster entrou com o processo em nome dos estudantes.","options":["The state government","The school board","The law firm Morrison & Foerster","The teachers'' union"],"prompt":"Who represented the students in the lawsuit?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Na segunda-feira, o juiz disse que emitiria uma liminar contra o teste, a menos que os advogados do estado apresentassem uma argumentação convincente.","options":["Dismiss the case","Issue an injunction against the test","Order the test to be given","Rule in favor of the state"],"prompt":"What did Judge Freedman initially say he would do on Monday?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O juiz adiou a decisão para sexta-feira, dando mais tempo para os advogados do estado apresentarem seus argumentos.","options":["To allow more students to take the test","To give the state''s attorneys more time to argue","To wait for new evidence from the plaintiffs","To consult with other judges"],"prompt":"Why did Judge Freedman delay his decision until Friday?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"O superintendente estadual informou que cerca de 47.000 seniores ainda precisavam passar no teste.","options":["Approximately 47,000","Nearly 90,000","About 87,000","Exactly 32"],"prompt":"How many seniors were affected by the potential ruling?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Críticos viam o exame como uma barreira que castigava estudantes por circunstâncias fora de seu controle, como falta de recursos.","options":["It was too expensive to administer","It added too much stress to students","It punished students for factors beyond their control","It did not align with the school curriculum"],"prompt":"What were the critics'' main argument against the exam?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"O atraso foi visto como um momento para o estado reconsiderar e para o público discutir a justiça na educação.","options":["A victory for the state","A need for more testing","A moment for reconsideration and public discussion","A failure of the legal system"],"prompt":"What did the judge''s delay symbolize in the broader context?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto menciona que os dias de espera foram cheios de ansiedade e esperança para os envolvidos.","options":["Indifferent","Anxious and hopeful","Angry and violent","Excited and confident"],"prompt":"What was the attitude of the students and educators while waiting for the decision?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
