insert into public.quick_lessons (id, language, level, title, body, question, options, answer_index, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-quick-lesson-en-b2-d2d76cab26bf', 'en', 'B2', 'Connecting Ideas: Discourse Markers for Argumentative Writing', 'Have you ever read an opinion piece and felt that the writer''s argument was disjointed, or that the connection between ideas was unclear? Often, the problem lies not in the content, but in the lack of effective discourse markers. These are words and phrases that act as signposts, guiding the reader through your reasoning. For Brazilian learners of English, mastering these markers is key to producing clear, persuasive texts and engaging in sophisticated discussions.

Consider the difference between saying "I think we should reduce car use in cities. Air pollution is a problem." and "I think we should reduce car use in cities, as air pollution is a serious issue. Moreover, it would improve public health." The second version flows better, sounds more authoritative, and explicitly shows the logical relationship between ideas. This is the power of discourse markers.

Discourse markers can be categorized by their function. Some, like ''in addition'', ''furthermore'', and ''moreover'', add information. Others, such as ''however'', ''on the other hand'', and ''nevertheless'', introduce a contrast. Then there are those that signal cause and effect: ''therefore'', ''as a result'', ''consequently''. You also have markers for giving examples (''for instance'', ''such as'') and for concluding (''in conclusion'', ''to sum up'').

In academic and formal writing, these markers are essential. They demonstrate that you can manage complex ideas and present them coherently. For example, an essay might say, "Many argue that remote work increases productivity. However, this is not always the case, as some employees struggle with isolation. Therefore, a hybrid model might be the best solution." Here, ''however'' signals a counterpoint, and ''therefore'' introduces the logical outcome.

It''s also important to understand that these markers have different levels of formality. While ''but'' and ''so'' are perfectly acceptable in casual conversation, ''nevertheless'' and ''consequently'' are more appropriate for written reports or formal speeches. Using the wrong register can make your writing seem too casual or too stiff. For B2 level, you should be comfortable using a range of markers in both spoken and written English.

Finally, remember that more is not always better. Overusing discourse markers can make your writing sound mechanical and repetitive. The goal is to use them strategically to guide your reader, not to fill every sentence. As you practice, you''ll develop a sense of when a marker is needed and which one is most effective. This will elevate your English from simply correct to truly compelling.', 'Which discourse marker best introduces an additional point that supports the main argument?', '["However","Furthermore","Therefore","In contrast"]'::jsonb, 1, '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"''Furthermore'' é usado para adicionar informação que apoia o mesmo argumento. ''However'' e ''In contrast'' introduzem contraste, e ''Therefore'' introduz consequência.","options":["However","Furthermore","Therefore","In contrast"],"prompt":"Which discourse marker best introduces an additional point that supports the main argument?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"''As a result'' indica uma consequência: a queda dos lucros levou ao corte de custos. ''On the other hand'' é para contraste, ''For example'' para exemplo, e ''In addition'' para adicionar.","options":["On the other hand","For example","As a result","In addition"],"prompt":"In the sentence ''The company''s profits fell sharply. ____, they decided to cut costs.'', which marker fits best?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"''Nevertheless'' é usado para contrastar, geralmente após um ponto e vírgula ou ponto final. A opção B mostra a pausa correta. As outras opções têm pontuação ou ordem de palavras incorretas.","options":["Nevertheless, she was tired, she finished the work.","She was tired; nevertheless, she finished the work.","She was tired nevertheless finished the work.","She finished the work, nevertheless she was tired."],"prompt":"Which sentence correctly uses ''nevertheless''?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"''Therefore'' é um marcador formal que indica conclusão ou consequência. ''Then'', ''And'' e ''Plus'' são mais informais.","options":["Therefore","Then","And","Plus"],"prompt":"Choose the most formal alternative to ''so'' in the sentence ''The evidence was clear, so they changed the policy.''"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"''For instance'' é usado para introduzir um exemplo. As outras opções indicam consequência, contraste e adição.","options":["Many countries have implemented similar policies. For instance, Germany and France.","Many countries have implemented similar policies. Consequently, Germany and France.","Many countries have implemented similar policies. However, Germany and France.","Many countries have implemented similar policies. In addition, Germany and France."],"prompt":"Which sentence uses a discourse marker to give an example?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
