values ('generated-quick-lesson-en-b2-f225517bd93b', 'en', 'B2', 'Argumentative Discourse Markers for B2', 'Argumentative discourse markers are words and phrases that help you structure your arguments, show relationships between ideas, and guide your reader or listener through your reasoning. They are essential for clear and persuasive communication, whether you''re writing an essay, participating in a debate, or simply discussing an issue with friends. In this lesson, we''ll explore some common markers of contrast, addition, cause and effect, and conclusion.

We use contrast markers to introduce an idea that opposes or qualifies a previous point. Words like ''however'', ''on the other hand'', and ''nevertheless'' signal a shift in direction. For example, you might say, ''The new policy has many benefits. However, it may also create some challenges.'' These markers help you acknowledge complexity and show that you''ve considered different perspectives.

Addition markers, such as ''furthermore'', ''moreover'', and ''in addition'', allow you to build on your argument by presenting supporting points. They strengthen your case by showing that you have more than one reason. For instance, ''The new policy is cost-effective. Furthermore, it will improve employee satisfaction.'' This makes your argument more robust and convincing.

Cause and effect markers, like ''therefore'', ''consequently'', and ''as a result'', link a reason to its outcome. They are crucial for logical reasoning. For example, ''The company failed to invest in new technology. Consequently, it lost its competitive edge.'' These markers make your arguments clear and show that you can think critically about consequences.

Conclusion markers, such as ''in conclusion'', ''to sum up'', and ''ultimately'', signal that you are wrapping up your argument. They help summarize your main points and leave a lasting impression. For example, ''In conclusion, the evidence strongly suggests that renewable energy is the best path forward.'' These markers are especially important in formal writing, but they also appear in spoken discourse.

As you practice using discourse markers, remember to choose the marker that best fits the logical relationship you want to express. Overusing or misusing them can make your speech sound unnatural. Also, be aware that some markers are more formal than others. For instance, ''nevertheless'' is more formal than ''but''. In academic writing, markers like ''furthermore'' and ''consequently'' are common, while in casual conversation, we might use ''also'' and ''so''.

To improve your use of discourse markers, read academic articles and opinion pieces in English. Notice how the writers connect their ideas. Try to use these markers in your own writing and speaking. Don''t be afraid to experiment, but always check that your marker accurately reflects the relationship between your ideas. Remember, the goal is to make your argument clear, logical, and persuasive.', 'What is the main purpose of argumentative discourse markers?', '["To make sentences longer and more complex.","To structure arguments and show relationships between ideas.","To replace all punctuation marks.","To make the text more difficult to understand."]'::jsonb, 1, '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Marcadores discursivos argumentativos têm a função de estruturar argumentos e mostrar relações lógicas entre ideias, como contraste, adição, causa e consequência, e conclusão.","options":["To make sentences longer and more complex.","To structure arguments and show relationships between ideas.","To replace all punctuation marks.","To make the text more difficult to understand."],"prompt":"What is the main purpose of argumentative discourse markers?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"However é um marcador de contraste, usado para introduzir uma ideia que se opõe à anterior. Furthermore e In addition são de adição, e Therefore é de consequência.","options":["Furthermore","Therefore","However","In addition"],"prompt":"Which marker is best to introduce an opposing idea?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Consequently indica consequência: estudar duro foi a causa e passar no exame foi a consequência. However indica contraste, enquanto in addition e moreover indicam adição.","options":["She studied hard; however, she passed the exam.","She studied hard; consequently, she passed the exam.","She studied hard; in addition, she passed the exam.","She studied hard; moreover, she passed the exam."],"prompt":"Choose the sentence that correctly uses a cause-and-effect marker."},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"In conclusion é usado para concluir e resumir os pontos principais. Moreover é de adição, on the other hand de contraste e consequently de consequência.","options":["Moreover","On the other hand","In conclusion","Consequently"],"prompt":"Which marker is typically used to summarize an argument?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Therefore indica consequência lógica: o tempo ruim foi a causa, e ficar em casa foi a consequência. However seria contraste, e furthermore/moreover são adição.","options":["However","Therefore","Furthermore","Moreover"],"prompt":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate marker: ''The weather was terrible. _____, we decided to stay home.''"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
